Package: fullmetaphone
Type: Package
Title: Full-Length Metaphone and Double Metaphone Phonetic Codes
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Anil Kumar", "Goyal", email = "anilyayavar@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre", "cph")),
    person("Atharv", "Tyagi", email = "tatharv597@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cph")),
    person("Lawrence", "Philips", role = "ctb",
           comment = "Designer of the Metaphone and Double Metaphone algorithms and author of their original code"),
    person("Maurice", "Aubrey", role = "ctb",
           comment = "Author of the C implementation of Double Metaphone whose rules are followed here"),
    person("Kevin", "Atkinson", role = "ctb",
           comment = "Bug fixes to that C implementation"),
    person("The Apache Software Foundation", role = "cph",
           comment = "Apache Commons Codec, the basis of metaphone() and of the test data")
    )
Description: Encodes names and words into phonetic codes using the
    Metaphone algorithm (Philips 1990, "Hanging on the Metaphone",
    Computer Language 7(12)) and the Double Metaphone algorithm (Philips
    2000, "The Double Metaphone Search Algorithm", C/C++ Users Journal
    18(6)). Names that sound alike but are spelled differently get the
    same code. Codes are returned in full rather than cut to the first
    four characters, so long and multi-part names stay distinguishable.
    Useful for record linkage, de-duplication and audit of name fields.
